---
args: {"update": "DispatchUpdate", "dispatchBook": "DeliveryRecoveryBook | null"}
returns: "ShipmentRepair"
---
1. Bind prior to dispatchBook or DeliveryRecoveryBook { revision: 0, legs: [], reservations: [], promises: [], deliveredShipmentIds: [], consumedNoticeIds: [] }. Bind orders to update.orders or an empty collection. Bind reservations = reconcileCarrierTransactions(prior.reservations, update.notices, update.reservationReceipts or an empty collection). Process operation receipts before offering any capacity again; an unknown cancellation leaves its capacity occupied.
2. Bind delta = interpretClassScopedDisruption(update, prior). Bind promises = recoverDistinctAppointments(update.orders or an empty collection, prior.promises, update.notices, update.priorityRules). Preserve each shipment's separate delivery deadlines and dependent installation appointments.
3. Identify only legs dependent on changed offers, class eligibility, handling capability or reservation outcomes. Preserve all other leg and promise records. A partial route reopening applies only to established eligible classes, never to an uncertain reopening time.
4. For each affected shipment call enumerateHandlingSafePaths(order, update.routeOffers or an empty collection, delta, reservations), collecting the returned alternatives. Generate reroute, split or consolidation alternatives only from supplied capabilities and offered capacity.
5. Bind allocated = allocateScarceLegs(alternatives, orders, reservations, update.priorityRules). Bind reviewedPromises = qualifyRevisedPromises(allocated, promises, reservations, update.notices). Do not promise the last slot to two planners, or call recovery complete because a booking was accepted.
6. Bind proposedReservations to the exact requests needed by allocated feasible legs, with offer identities, expected offer versions, shipment IDs, quantity and state requested; absent capacity or quantity leaves a task instead of a fabricated request. Bind nextBook as DeliveryRecoveryBook { revision: advance only for new source/receipt/plan facts, legs: allocated plus unaffected prior legs, reservations: reconciled reservations plus each new request once by operationId, promises: reviewedPromises plus unaffected historical promises, deliveredShipmentIds: prior IDs plus only actual matched delivery observations, consumedNoticeIds: prior IDs plus the exact processed notice IDs once }. Return ShipmentRepair { dispatchBook: nextBook, revisedLegs: allocated, proposedReservations, customerCorrections: the actual changed or unsupported promises, recoveryTasks: remaining handling, acceptance and delivery tasks, unresolvedCapacity: unknown reservations, failed release confirmations and capacity conflicts }. Preserve rejected bookings and unknown outcomes. Close a task only when actual carrier progress and approved customer commitments agree.
